[statement]
As `a-condition-of-negated-entries-alone-needs-a-package-it-names`, where
a package of the name could be installed and is not: `f`'s condition is
`!a<2`; `a` 3, which provides `d` at no version, is a candidate for `d`
and passed over for `d` 1, and apk installs `d` alone. Installed at a
version the entry does not forbid, `a` would complete the condition
(`install-order/install-if-a-negated-entry-the-package-placed-escapes-triggers`).

